.TH mnnn-code 1  "mnnn-code 2.11.2" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-code \- Code spaces: math, Polars, Rust or Python (or a prebuilt plugin) compiled into a native plugin that reads and writes your data and shows a result
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn code\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Code spaces: math, Polars, Rust or Python (or a prebuilt plugin) compiled into a native plugin that reads and writes your data and shows a result
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Every language becomes a native plugin (a Rust cdylib built with cargo, cached by content hash
under MUNINN_HOME/code); a prebuilt plugin (\-\-lang plugin, the source is its path) loads as is.
Python goes through Rython (rythonc on PATH or MUNINN_RYTHONC). Without a Rust toolchain only
prebuilt plugins run; `mnnn code check` says what is missing.
.PP
A code space runs as native code with your rights. Before its first run, and after every change,
review it and approve it (`approve`, or `run \-y`). Imported code spaces need approving again.
.PP
Input: \-\-model MODEL [\-\-where "FIELD OP VALUE"]… [\-\-matching TEXT] [\-\-group F] [\-\-sort F|\-F]
[\-\-limit N]; plugins can load, create and update any model (bars too), and create models.
.PP
Examples:
  mnnn code create fast \-\-lang math \-\-model bars \-\-where "symbol = BTC/USDT" \-\-group symbol \-\-file fast.mth
  mnnn code run fast \-y
  mnnn code create spread \-\-lang python \-\-source $'def spread(high: float, low: float) \-> float:\en    return high \- low'
  mnnn rule create on\-import \-\-on import \-\-then "run\-code fast"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-code\-create(1)
Create a code space (not approved to run yet)
.TP
mnnn\-code\-edit(1)
Change a code space; a new source needs approving again
.TP
mnnn\-code\-list(1)
List code spaces
.TP
mnnn\-code\-show(1)
Show a code space: its source, input, approval and last run
.TP
mnnn\-code\-remove(1)
Remove a code space (asks first)
.TP
mnnn\-code\-approve(1)
Approve a code space\*(Aqs current source to run
.TP
mnnn\-code\-build(1)
Compile a code space (cached: nothing happens when it is built already)
.TP
mnnn\-code\-run(1)
Run a code space: build if needed, then run it and show its result
.TP
mnnn\-code\-check(1)
Check a code space (or, without one, the toolchains) without running anything
.TP
mnnn\-code\-sdk(1)
Write the plugin SDK (the `muninn\-plugin` crate) to build prebuilt plugins with
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
